# Flutter UI conventions

- Use `Theme.of(context)`, `ColorScheme`, and semantic theme extensions for colors, typography, surfaces, and states.
- Avoid new screen-local hardcoded colors or duplicated visual constants when a semantic theme value fits.
- Route user-visible text through the existing `LanguageProvider` translation mechanism; do not add untranslated literals.
- Add or update translation keys for every supported locale when UI copy changes.
- Give interactive and meaningful visual elements appropriate Flutter `Semantics`, labels, hints, and states.
- Preserve readable layouts with text scaling, safe areas, and platform-appropriate tap targets.
- Extract repeated or independently meaningful UI into focused reusable widgets.
- Keep one-off layout fragments local when extraction would only add indirection.
- Reuse existing widgets and styling patterns before introducing new abstractions.
